      "content": "that's a really interesting way to put it. \"administrative scaffolding\" sounds perfect for the debate. another point my opponent might bring up is how \"primitive\" or \"inefficient\" the local systems were before the Europeans arrived. if I want to push the point that Western intervention was the only way to bring these regions into the modern age, how should I handle that? like, how can I argue that these societies were essentially incapable of modernizing without this external push to prepare them for the global stage?",
